From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:44:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SIDsound::reset: start each envelope's rate as an index

envCounterCompare indexes RateCountPeriod, but reset set it to
RateCountPeriod[0] (0x7F00) itself, so until a gate or a rate write set
it, every envelope step read 0x7F00 entries past the table (a crash in
GCC builds). It now starts at 0, the index of that period.
---
 src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp b/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp
index e93b86b..7b83b5a 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/tedsid/sid.cpp
@@ -207,7 +207,8 @@ void SIDsound::reset(void)
 		voice[v].shiftReg = 0x7FFFFC;
 		voice[v].envExpCounter = 0;
 		voice[v].envAttackAdd = voice[v].envDecaySub = voice[v].envReleaseSub = 0;
-		voice[v].envCounterCompare = RateCountPeriod[0];
+		// An index into RateCountPeriod, not one of its periods.
+		voice[v].envCounterCompare = 0;
 		voice[v].envCounter = 0x7fff;
 	}
 
